
# Driver Microservice — Ride Sharing System

## 1. Project Overview

Driver Microservice manages:
- Driver registration and profile management
- Driver account status
- Driver verification
- Driver availability
- Driver GPS location
- Nearby driver searching
- Vehicle registration and management

## 2. Technology Stack

- Java 17
- Spring Boot
- Spring Data JPA
- PostgreSQL
- Maven
- Eclipse IDE
- Postman

## 3. Application Configuration

Application Port: 8082

Database: driver_db

Base URL:
http://localhost:8082/api/v1/drivers

## 4. How to Run

1. Start PostgreSQL.
2. Ensure driver_db exists.
3. Configure the DB_PASSWORD environment variable.
4. Open driver-service in Eclipse.
5. Run DriverServiceApplication.java.
6. Verify the service starts on port 8082.

## 5. Driver API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| POST | /api/v1/drivers | Register driver |
| GET | /api/v1/drivers | Get all drivers |
| GET | /api/v1/drivers/{id} | Get driver by ID |
| PUT | /api/v1/drivers/{id} | Update driver |
| DELETE | /api/v1/drivers/{id} | Delete driver |
| GET | /api/v1/drivers/search | Search driver |
| PATCH | /api/v1/drivers/{id}/location | Update location |
| PATCH | /api/v1/drivers/{id}/availability | Update availability |
| PATCH | /api/v1/drivers/{id}/account-status | Update account status |
| PATCH | /api/v1/drivers/{id}/verification | Verify driver |
| GET | /api/v1/drivers/nearby | Search nearby drivers |

## 6. Vehicle API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| POST | /api/v1/drivers/{id}/vehicles | Register vehicle |
| GET | /api/v1/drivers/{id}/vehicles | Get vehicles |
| GET | /api/v1/drivers/{id}/vehicles/{vehicleId} | Get vehicle |
| PUT | /api/v1/drivers/{id}/vehicles/{vehicleId} | Update vehicle |
| DELETE | /api/v1/drivers/{id}/vehicles/{vehicleId} | Delete vehicle |

## 7. Postman Testing

### Test 1: Register Driver

Method: POST

URL:
http://localhost:8082/api/v1/drivers

Request Body:
```json
{
  "name": "Rahul Sharma",
  "email": "rahul.driver@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "licenseNumber": "DL0420260012345",
  "latitude": 28.7041,
  "longitude": 77.1025
}
```

Expected:
- HTTP 201 Created
- accountStatus = ACTIVE
- availabilityStatus = OFFLINE
- verificationStatus = PENDING

Save the generated driver ID for later tests.

### Test 2: Get Driver By ID

Method: GET

URL:
http://localhost:8082/api/v1/drivers/1

Expected: HTTP 200 OK

### Test 3: Get All Drivers

Method: GET

URL:
http://localhost:8082/api/v1/drivers?page=0&size=10

Expected: HTTP 200 OK

### Test 4: Search By Email

Method: GET

URL:
http://localhost:8082/api/v1/drivers/search?email=rahul.driver@example.com

Expected: HTTP 200 OK

### Test 5: Register Vehicle

Method: POST

URL:
http://localhost:8082/api/v1/drivers/1/vehicles

Request Body:
```json
{
  "vehicleNumber": "DL01AB1234",
  "vehicleType": "CAR",
  "model": "Maruti Suzuki Dzire",
  "color": "White"
}
```

Expected: HTTP 201 Created

### Test 6: Verify Driver

Method: PATCH

URL:
http://localhost:8082/api/v1/drivers/1/verification?status=VERIFIED

Expected:
- HTTP 200 OK
- verificationStatus = VERIFIED

### Test 7: Update Driver Location

Method: PATCH

URL:
http://localhost:8082/api/v1/drivers/1/location

Request Body:
```json
{
  "latitude": 28.7041,
  "longitude": 77.1025
}
```

Expected:
- HTTP 200 OK
- New locationUpdatedAt timestamp

### Test 8: Make Driver ONLINE

Method: PATCH

URL:
http://localhost:8082/api/v1/drivers/1/availability?status=ONLINE

Expected:
- HTTP 200 OK
- availabilityStatus = ONLINE

Prerequisites:
- ACTIVE account
- VERIFIED driver
- Registered vehicle
- Recent GPS update

### Test 9: Nearby Drivers

Method: GET

URL:
http://localhost:8082/api/v1/drivers/nearby?latitude=28.7041&longitude=77.1025&radiusKm=5

Expected:
- HTTP 200 OK
- List of eligible nearby drivers
- distanceKm included in each result

### Test 10: Block Driver

Method: PATCH

URL:
http://localhost:8082/api/v1/drivers/1/account-status?status=BLOCKED

Expected:
- HTTP 200 OK
- accountStatus = BLOCKED
- availabilityStatus = OFFLINE

## 8. Negative Test Cases

| Test | Expected Status |
|------|-----------------|
| Duplicate email | 409 Conflict |
| Duplicate license number | 409 Conflict |
| Invalid email | 400 Bad Request |
| Invalid phone number | 400 Bad Request |
| Invalid latitude | 400 Bad Request |
| Missing driver ID | 404 Not Found |
| Invalid search radius | 400 Bad Request |
| ONLINE without verification | 400 Bad Request |
| Duplicate vehicle number | 409 Conflict |

## 9. PostgreSQL Verification

Check registered drivers:

```sql
SELECT * FROM drivers;
```

Check registered vehicles:

```sql
SELECT * FROM vehicles;
```

## 10. Important Development Notes

- Driver registration defaults to ACTIVE, OFFLINE, PENDING.
- Driver must be VERIFIED before becoming ONLINE.
- Driver requires at least one vehicle.
- GPS location must have been updated within 10 minutes.
- Nearby searching uses the Haversine formula.
- ON_RIDE will be handled by the future Ride Microservice.
- Account and verification status endpoints require admin authorization before production use.
- Protect driver contact information and exact location with authentication and authorization.

## 11. Next Development Steps

- Add automated integration tests
- Add authentication and authorization
- Add Flyway migrations
- Add driver assignment/reservation API
- Integrate with Ride Microservice
